+## Session update (2026-10-09, part 3): fork-vs-upstream audit — what `juspay/hyperswitch` has that ours does not
+
+This session added `juspay/hyperswitch` as a second remote (`upstream`, fetch
+only — we never push to it) and measured the divergence for the first time.
+
+**Where the two trees stand (2026-10-09):**
+
+- `upstream/main` tip fetched: `39c040c83015` (a plain feature/fix tip, not a
+  release tag — the latest `chore(version)` commit nearby is `2026.10.09.0`).
+- merge-base with our `main`: `15c4865d91` ("fix(router): correct field mapping
+  in browse offers response (#14141)").
+- **226 upstream commits we do not have; 353 of our commits are not upstream.**
+  We are not tracking upstream in any automated way, so this gap only ever
+  grows. Nothing below is a merge plan — it is the raw list of upstream work
+  worth pulling in, triaged.
+
+**Method (so a future session can redo it):**
+
+```bash
+git remote add upstream https://github.com/juspay/hyperswitch.git   # fetch only
+git fetch --filter=blob:none upstream main
+git rev-list --count HEAD..upstream/main          # 226 behind
+git --no-pager log --oneline $(git merge-base HEAD upstream/main)..upstream/main
+```
+
+Caveat on the "have/miss" checks below: upstream UCs are functionally
+de-duplicated, so a feature can exist upstream in a file we never added. A
+`MISS` means the *named* symbol/feature is absent from our tree, not that the
+capability is impossible.
+
+### Confirmed gaps (grepped for the symbol, absent from our tree)
+
+1. **Wero wallet payment method** — no `Wero` anywhere in `crates/`. A new
+   payment method + connector support we simply don't have.
+2. **Preferred-connector routing for Interac** — "pin the customer's last
+   successful connector"; no `preferred_connector` in our tree. Sits close to
+   the routing work below.
+3. **UCS `shadow_rollout_percent`** — split shadow traffic from primary
+   independently; no `shadow_rollout_percent` in our tree.
+4. **Merchant alert read permission** — new permission; no `merchant_alert`.
+5. **OCI Vault KMS backend** — a third secrets/encryption backend (alongside
+   AWS KMS and GCP KMS); no `oci_vault`/`OciVault` in our tree. Only relevant
+   if we ever run on Oracle Cloud; low priority otherwise.
+6. **Payments "create context s2s"** — a server-to-server context creation
+   path; no `context_s2s`/`ContextS2S` in our tree.
+7. **`rapid_dispute_resolution`** — Stripe webhook → dispute
+   `additional_details`; absent.
+
+### Categories to port (present upstream, need a real diff before we call them gaps)
+
+**Routing / orchestration**
+- Move dynamic routing decisions to the Decision Engine.
+- Eligibility filtering for fallback connectors in hybrid routing.
+- Preferred-connector routing (Interac) — see gap 1 above.
+- Generic capture-method handling upgraded to auto-fallback.
+- External-vault-proxy: core orchestration, execution contract, and
+  (payouts) execution via UCS — three separate upstream commits. Touches the
+  same vault/payouts path this fork already carries fixes in.
+- `deja` pin: upstream moved it "past the addressing fix" and named the
+  concurrent address forks — direct overlap with our own deja pin, worth
+  reading before any future diesel/deja bump.
+
+**Storage / cache / perf**
+- `perf(cache)`: hold redis entries past in-memory lifetime with jitter;
+  coordinate in-memory cache population per key.
+- `perf(merchant_connector_account)`: cache MCA list queries via scope supersets.
+- `perf(payment-methods)`: pay-then-vault using redis.
+- `refactor(cache)`: make in-memory caches runtime-configurable and store-owned.
+- `refactor(payments)`: optimize `get_trackers` in the create flow.
+- `fix(storage)`: avoid unnecessary DB connection leases in write operations.
+- `refactor(storage_impl)`: move `Conversion` impls for payment_attempt, MCA,
+  and merchant_account into `storage_impl` — three commits, same crate we are
+  actively working in for Task 73/a, so these will conflict and should be
+  read, not cherry-picked blind.
+
+**CI (mirror-safety check, since this fork's CI diverged hard)**
+- `perf(ci)`: bulk-restore sccache cache to speed builds — upstream solved the
+  same caching problem we re-solved locally this session.
+- `ci`: trim redundant compile steps and rework the S3 sccache backend.
+- If we ever re-sync the `crates/` baseline, re-read these before trusting the
+  current `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
+
+**Payments / refunds / disputes / webhooks (non-connector fixes)**
+- Update the connector mandate id on the payment method irrespective of
+  active/inactive; return the saved connector mandate id in responses.
+- Align refund connector error mapping with payments.
+- Defer bank-redirect payment-method creation until terminal status.
+- Schedule a Payment Sync workflow after PaymentsCapture; update the existing
+  PAYMENTS_SYNC process tracker instead of creating a duplicate.
+- Sum connector latency across retry attempts.
+- Skip vault delete for PMs never stored in the vault.
+- Handle concurrent duplicate dispute-webhook inserts.
+- Prefer parent payment reference / merchant txn id for UCS dispute and
+  webhook-bridge lookups.
+- Return saved connector mandate ID and propagate card_network for wallet
+  payment attempts.
+
+**Security / correctness**
+- `fix(encryption)`: stop misclassifying AES-GCM ciphertext as remote
+  key-manager format — security-adjacent, take seriously.
+- `fix: install rustls CryptoProvider` before GCP KMS client construction.
+- `fix(router)`: validate URLs.
+- `fix(superposition)`: validate proxy org and workspace headers against the
+  configured scope; require all scoping dimensions in proxy requests.
+- `fix(scheduler)`: reuse the redis consumer across polls.
+- `fix(email)`: route SMTP sends through the configured proxy.
+- `fix(analytics)`: keep spaces in filter values.
+
+**Connectors (large, and our connector set is bespoke — do NOT bulk-port)**
+- ~70 upstream connector commits (fixes and features) the fork does not have.
+  Upstream also registers many new UCS-only connectors we don't carry
+  (Shift4, Elavon PG, PayNearMe, JP Morgan Orbital, Saferpay, D24 WebPay,
+  Global Payments Heartland, Pay.com, GlobalPay, Etisalat, Merchante, Datatrans,
+  Fiserv Commerce Hub, Revolv3, Santander Pix webhooks, Trustly returning-user
+  flow, etc.). **Out of scope as a bulk port** — our fork keeps ten specific
+  providers and a custom connector layer; this list is for lookup only when one
+  overlaps a provider we actually use.
+
+### Explicitly out of scope for this fork
+
+- The ~14 upstream Cypress-test commits and the ~7 Postman/Docs commits — our
+  test surface is different and these would be noise.
+- Bulk-importing upstream's UCS-only connector registry.
+- The `chore(version)` release-numbering commits and `prism` version bumps.
+
+### Recommended next actions (ordered)
+
+1. **Read `fix(encryption)` and the `superposition` header-validation fixes
+   first** — they are small, security-relevant, and mostly self-contained.
+2. **Read the `storage_impl` `Conversion` moves** before the next Task 73/a
+   session, so that work is planned against the upstream shape rather than
+   diverging further.
+3. **Adopt upstream's two CI caching commits** as reference for our own CI
+   (we currently have a hand-rolled equivalent; reconcile, don't double up).
+4. **Pick the routing set** (Decision Engine, fallback eligibility,
+   preferred-connector, shadow rollout) as the next feature-sized chunk — it
+   is the largest coherent block and overlaps Task 77's connector work.
+5. Leave the connector bulk-port and the Wero payment method as
+   **deliberately deferred** until a product decision says we need them.
